# Executable scripts keep LF, whatever the checkout does to everything else.
#
# core.autocrlf is true here and there was no .gitattributes, so a FRESH
# checkout - a worktree, a clone, a new machine - rewrote scripts/db-push.mjs
# with CRLF. A shebang line ending in \r stops the file parsing at all, and
# scripts/db-push.test.ts then failed to load with "Invalid or unexpected
# token". The main checkout was fine only because those files were written with
# LF and never checked out again, which is why nobody had seen it.
#
# Scoped deliberately to executable script types rather than `* text=auto`:
# renormalising every file in the repo is a far larger change than this problem
# warrants, and would collide with work in progress elsewhere.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
